markdown <<MARKDOWN
# Introducing Functions in JavaScript

#### When building web apps, you often want the same action to happen in multiple places, such as updating a score when different buttons are clicked.

#### Instead of rewriting the same code each time, we can use a function.

<div style="background-color: #B7E0E5; border-radius: 10px; padding: 15px; margin: 20px auto; max-width: 85%; box-sizing: border-box;">
<p style="font-size: 14pt; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 120%;">📖 <strong>Function</strong> is a named set of reusable instructions that tells your program what to do.</p>
</div>

---

<img src="https://images.code.org/f32fe913796b205f37f92bc782e5d0f0-image-1772209777254.png" alt="javascript code without function" width="275px" style="border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 0px 40px 10px 20px;">

## Before: Repeating Code

#### This code works. But look closely.

#### In both button actions, we:
- ####  Change the value of `total`
- #### Update the display

#### The same steps appear more than once. If we wanted to change how the total is shown, we would need to update it in multiple places.

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

---

<img src="https://images.code.org/41b9f258f08f7f541b34b220550be557-image-1772209834211.png" alt="javascript code with function" width="275px" style="border-radius:10px; float:right; margin: 40px 40px 10px 20px;">


## After: Using a Function

#### We moved the repeated steps into a function called `updateTotal()`.

#### Now each button simply calls the function.

#### The shared logic lives in one place, which makes the code:
- #### Shorter
- #### Easier to read
- #### Easier to update

#### If we change how the total is displayed, we only edit the function.

<div style="clear:both;"></div>

---

## Quick Check 

<p style="font-size: 14pt;"><strong>Question:</strong><br>
If you wanted to change how the total is displayed, where would you make the change?</p>

<details>
  <summary style="font-size:16pt; font-weight:bold; cursor:pointer; background-color:#f7f8fa; padding:10px; border-radius:6px;">
    🔎 Check your Answer
  </summary>

  <div style="margin-top:12px; font-size:14pt; background-color:#f7f8fa; padding:12px; border-radius:6px;">
    <p style ="font-size: 14pt;" ><strong>Answer:</strong><br>
    Inside the <code style="font-size:12pt;">updateTotal()</code> function, because that is where the display logic is defined. 
    Since all buttons call this function, we only need to update the code in one place.</p>
  </div>

</details>

## Next Up

#### Let’s create our own functions.
MARKDOWN
